@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Upload buffer pool regressions
+
+Run from any directory with Python 3 and a C++23 compiler:
+
+```
+python3 tests/regression/upload_buffer_pool/run.py
+python3 tests/regression/upload_buffer_pool/run.py --sanitize
+```
+
+`CXX` selects the compiler. The sanitizer option requires AddressSanitizer and
+UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer support. If LeakSanitizer is unavailable under a
+traced container, `ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0` disables only leak detection;
+`edge_tests.cpp` separately checks tracked page destruction.
+
+The generic pool tests compile the production `.cpp` and SDK headers directly.
+They cover normal allocation, initial/repeated allocation failure, page rollover,
+reclaim/retry, partial requests, alignment, flush ranges, list ownership,
+timeline changes and page destruction.
+
+`check_d3d_ownership.py` compiles the exact production page-creation method body
+against deterministic COM/device test doubles. It checks creation failure, Map
+failure and successful page ownership. Its optional argument is a source file
+for negative-control testing. This is not a Windows D3D runtime/device test.
+
+These tests require no game data and do not launch the game.
